    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1956014398893330584",
      "url": "https://x.com/followlastma/status/1956014398893330584",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/followlastma/status/1956014398893330584",
      "text": "[4:22PM] #OkotaIsolo #TrafficUpdate \n\nTraffic on Daleko–Mushin Bridge is moving freely, as is the route from 5 Star to connect under the Iyana Isolo Bridge.\nIlasa through Ballet to Ijesha, inward Mile 2, is experiencing smooth flow. Movement from Oke-Afa Bridge to Pako is also fast in both directions.\n\nThe Pako–Akiti–Chemist–Ago Roundabout route remains free-flowing in both directions.\nCele Link Bridge traffic is light, and the stretch from Cele through Rain Oil–Ago Intersection to Ago Palace Way is also moving well, with a smooth return trip.\n\nIlasa–Transformer to Apata Junction is clear in both directions. Ibeh Road to Ago Roundabout is equally free-flowing.\nFrom Kogberegbe through Ire Akari, Ile Ibadan, Mustapha, Ishaga, College, Omonije, Aiye, Limca, and LASUTECH Roundabout, traffic is smooth in both directions.\n\nCurrently, there are no reports of impediments or obstructions, and our men are ensuring ease of traffic movement. \n\n#FollowLASTMA",
